WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.250
Sprig 0.1 Preview: the user starts local VPN capture.

00:04.250 --> 00:20.350
Android requests notification permission. The user allows notifications.

00:20.350 --> 00:39.460
Android displays the VPN connection request. The user confirms it.

00:39.460 --> 00:57.680
VPN capture is active. Sprig must continuously process live network traffic.

00:57.680 --> 01:14.500
A separate local test app completes 20 requests with zero errors while Sprig runs in the background.

01:14.500 --> 01:38.300
The ongoing notification shows that Sprig capture is active while another app is open.

01:38.300 --> 02:01.330
Returning to Sprig shows 20 captured requests and successful HTTP 200 responses. Demo endpoint details are masked.

02:01.330 --> 02:17.200
The user stops capture. Sprig returns to the offline state and the VPN indicator disappears.
